# Cursor Rule: No '@' Imports

## Purpose

This rule prohibits the use of '@' imports (e.g., import ... from '@/...') in the codebase to avoid ambiguity and potential issues with path resolution, tooling, or portability.

---

globs:

- "src/\*_/_.ts"
- "src/\*_/_.tsx"
- "src/\*_/_.js"
- "src/\*_/_.jsx"

alwaysApply: true

description: |
Do not use '@' imports (e.g., import ... from '@/...') anywhere in the codebase. Use relative or absolute imports as configured in your project instead. This ensures clarity and compatibility across different tools and environments.
description:
globs:
alwaysApply: false

---
